      "title": "Simplifying Expressions in Degrees Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "70b59840-6653-5fba-87c1-0ddd5ae73610",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin(x-90^\\circ)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ or $\\cos x$.\n\n$\\sin(x-90^\\circ)=$ {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the difference formula for sine:\n$$\n\\sin(u-v)=\\sin u\\cos v-\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\nApply it and substitute the exact special-angle values:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x-90^\\circ)&=\\sin x\\cos 90^\\circ-\\cos x\\sin 90^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\cdot\\left(0\\right)-\\cos x\\cdot\\left(1\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "8936634c-4534-550a-bb57-0d96100e8bc7",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
